  "starterCode": "from collections import defaultdict\ndef solve(orders):\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, mathematically sound implementation.\n\n### ⚡ Implementation\n```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ndef solve(orders):\n    # orders: [{\"country\": str, \"amount\": number}, ...]\n    s=defaultdict(float); n=defaultdict(int)\n    for o in orders: s[o[\"country\"]]+=o[\"amount\"]; n[o[\"country\"]]+=1\n    return {k:s[k]/n[k] for k in s}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$",
